WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.800
OpenAI is folding its separate work mode back into regular ChatGPT, and your usage limits are about to share one pool. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 215. DeepDive covers how those allowances get counted, then Adobe's photo editing agent, a wired look at hidden deepfake tools, and quick bits. Paid plus and pro plans currently keep three separate usage counters, trending topics reports. One meter watches ordinary chatting, one watches the work tab for bigger projects,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.400
and one watches Codex, a helper that writes computer code.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.920
The test puts casual talk and large projects in the same window, so a homework chat can

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.620
turn into a request for a website or a slide deck without changing screens.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.020
Picture the text app on your phone opening a whole spreadsheet inside the same conversation,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.120
or cropping a picture without hopping to another screen.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:57.680
Handy, yes, a heavy project can still drain the monthly cap sooner, so small questions later

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:58.480
have less room.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:05.640
Millions of students in hobbyists already open chat GPT every day for homework, creative writing, and quick questions.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.880
SA brainstorming and language practice may feel that cap more when the task gets big.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:17.900
Open AI says most users likely will not feel a change, and instant the speedy model remains uncapped.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.580
The trial is going out slowly and the company wants feedback before anything wider.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:27.540
Here, paid users may get an email or a notice inside the app if they are invited to the

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.220
small trial.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.420
Open Settings, then Usage, right now, and look at those split meters while they still

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:33.900
sit apart.

00:01:34.996 --> 00:01:40.416
Token Counting sits underneath every chat GPT reply, and a token is just a small chunk of

00:01:40.416 --> 00:01:40.796
text.

00:01:41.316 --> 00:01:42.956
Picture the data plan on your phone.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.696
Streaming a full movie burns a lot more than sending a few texts.

00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:50.656
Chat bots run on a usage allowance that follows that same spirit.

00:01:50.656 --> 00:01:55.996
Hit send, and the system chops your words into tokens, roughly one token per word.

00:01:56.536 --> 00:02:01.436
The reply gets chopped too, so a long answer costs more than a short one. Treat those

00:02:01.436 --> 00:02:06.416
chunks like bricks in a building set. A tiny question is a handful of bricks. A huge

00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:12.416
project is a whole castle. A more advanced model, or a messy multi-step task, burns through

00:02:12.416 --> 00:02:17.436
the pile faster. High-definition video eats a mobile plan quicker than a plain message,

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:23.176
and hard AI jobs follow that pattern. School printers often give you a monthly page quota.

00:02:23.656 --> 00:02:27.016
A fat report uses the stack faster than a one-page worksheet.

00:02:27.656 --> 00:02:34.636
Once you see replies as stacks of those little chunks, the usage meter feels as ordinary as a data plan you already know how to live with.

00:02:35.553 --> 00:02:41.853
Adobe Research built an AI agent named Edit Agent that edits photos the way a skilled Photoshop user would.

00:02:41.853 --> 00:02:47.633
The Dakota reports, an agent here means software that can choose steps on its own, not a single

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:50.073
filter that slaps the same look on every picture.

00:02:50.593 --> 00:02:55.973
It studies the photo, then reaches for a specialized tool, such as the clone stamp, which copies

00:02:55.973 --> 00:03:00.933
pixels from a clean spot to cover a blemish, like patching a stain with matching fabric.

00:03:01.433 --> 00:03:06.293
It can also grab an adjustment brush, which lightens or darkens just one area instead of

00:03:06.293 --> 00:03:06.893
the whole frame.

00:03:06.893 --> 00:03:12.233
It tries a few passes, then a language model, the next word predictor behind chat

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:16.933
bots picks the winner using real measurements of the picture, such as whether a scratch

00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:17.833
is actually gone.

00:03:18.473 --> 00:03:22.853
Future editors could feel less like hunting through menus and more like a helper who already

00:03:22.853 --> 00:03:24.133
knows which button to press.

00:03:24.693 --> 00:03:29.353
The research is still early, so you will not find edit agent as a finished product in your

00:03:29.353 --> 00:03:30.033
pocket today.

00:03:30.593 --> 00:03:35.473
You can still get a tiny taste in the free Photoshop Express app on your phone or on the web.

00:03:35.473 --> 00:03:41.493
Upload a photo, tap Healing or Adjust, and watch which specific fixes the app suggests.

00:03:41.993 --> 00:03:45.053
That suggestion is a baby version of a toolpicking helper.

00:03:46.061 --> 00:03:51.781
Everyday looking AI apps hid extra tools for violent or non-consensual fakes, and wired

00:03:51.781 --> 00:03:53.501
counted roughly 400 of them.

00:03:54.041 --> 00:03:59.221
Most were tied to Chinese language developers, and they dressed up as ordinary image generators

00:03:59.221 --> 00:04:00.121
or chat toys.

00:04:00.121 --> 00:04:05.241
A deep fake is a fake photo or video made with AI that looks like a real person.

00:04:05.781 --> 00:04:08.681
Non-consensual means that person never agreed to it.

00:04:09.121 --> 00:04:13.921
The apps used regular AI models then added secret prompts or extra buttons that slipped

00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:15.001
past safety filters.

00:04:15.541 --> 00:04:18.041
The built-in rules meant to block harmful requests.

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:23.061
Think of a vending machine that looks normal, then a hidden button on the back that unlocks

00:04:23.061 --> 00:04:23.961
a locked cabinet.

00:04:24.521 --> 00:04:29.381
Once a powerful image tool is out in the world, keeping every copy of its safe is genuinely

00:04:29.381 --> 00:04:33.821
which is why origin and recent reviews are worth a minute of your time.

00:04:34.361 --> 00:04:38.321
If an AI app promises uncensored or anything goes image generation,

00:04:38.861 --> 00:04:40.801
treat that as a red flag and walk away.

00:04:41.361 --> 00:04:44.681
Stick to well-known tools such as the official chat GPT app,

00:04:45.101 --> 00:04:47.701
Google's Gemini, or Claude on its official site,

00:04:48.141 --> 00:04:50.841
where safety settings and reporting options sit in the open.

00:04:51.797 --> 00:04:55.617
Open AI reported handing over information on more than 200 cases

00:04:55.617 --> 00:04:57.777
to police in the third quarter of 2026.

00:04:57.777 --> 00:05:03.717
According to PPC Land, most involve people trying to get the chatbot to help with harmful

00:05:03.717 --> 00:05:09.117
or illegal activities. The safety teams behind these chatbots are watching for serious misuse

00:05:09.117 --> 00:05:14.187
and working with authorities when they see it. Parents of a 31-year-old woman are suing

00:05:14.187 --> 00:05:20.527
open AI after her death. SSB Crack news reports. She had epilepsy, a condition that can cause

00:05:20.527 --> 00:05:25.787
seizures and reportedly followed a tapering schedule from chat GPT, a plan for slowly

00:05:25.787 --> 00:05:30.327
lowering a dose. She stopped her prescribed medication and later died from a seizure.

00:05:31.027 --> 00:05:35.247
Her family argues the AI should have included stronger warnings on health-related answers,

00:05:35.827 --> 00:05:40.087
and the lesson is blunt. A chatbot is a well-read classmate, not a doctor.

